# Campus Classroom Environment Variables

# Required: Flask session secret key
SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here

# Required: Campus API credentials
CLIENT_ID=your-campus-client-id
CLIENT_SECRET=your-campus-client-secret

# Required: Environment (development, staging, or production)
ENV=development

# Optional: Explicit Campus service base URLs (campus-api-python#53).
# Normally unnecessary — the client derives them from ENV: development →
# Railway dev deployments, staging → *.campus.nyjc.dev, production →
# *.campus.nyjc.app. Set these only to override (e.g. local services).
# CAMPUS_AUTH_URL=https://campusauth-development.up.railway.app
# CAMPUS_API_URL=https://campusapi-development.up.railway.app

# Required: Canonical public origin of THIS service (scheme://host[:port], no
# path), e.g. https://<classroom-dev-domain>. Used to build absolute URLs,
# including the OAuth callback that flask_campus generates as
# {PUBLIC_URL}/finalize_login. This exact callback must be registered on the
# campus client's redirect_uris (see AGENTS.md) BEFORE login is used.
# Note: HOSTNAME is a bind address for the dev server and is NOT used for URL
# generation (the legacy https://{HOSTNAME} fallback is removed by campus#652).
PUBLIC_URL=https://<classroom-dev-domain>

# Optional: origin of the campus-profile app that hosts the integrations
# page (the one-time Google Classroom connect UX, issue #30). Derived from
# ENV when unset, exactly like the service URLs above.
# CAMPUS_PROFILE_URL=https://campus-profile-development.up.railway.app
#
# NOTE: this app has NO Google OAuth config of its own. Classroom tokens
# come from campus.auth's token broker (the google.classroom vault client);
# the legacy GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID/GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET/WORKSPACE_DOMAIN vars
# were removed with the app's own OAuth flow (issue #30, 2026-10-03).

# Optional: audit trace producer (campus#816, issue #37). With
# AUDIT_TRACING_ENABLED=1, classroom requests are recorded as spans in
# the campus audit service and campus SDK calls made while handling a
# request land as child spans (audit waterfall shows which route fired
# each campus call). Requires AUDIT_API_KEY — a producer key with
# traces:write, minted per campus docs/audit-tracing.md § Minting and
# bootstrapping keys. Read once at app creation: flipping the flag is a
# redeploy, not a runtime change; ingestion is async and fail-safe.
# AUDIT_TRACING_ENABLED=1
# AUDIT_API_KEY=audit_v1_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Optional: Server configuration
HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0
PORT=5000

# Optional: document-type questions (#78) — interactive single-file HTML
# documents stored with the assignment and served from a DEDICATED app
# hosting origin (`campus-apphost`, #81), never this app's own origin.
# On the MAIN deployment set EMBED_ORIGIN to the apphost deployment's
# public origin (unset = document questions render a "not available"
# notice on /a/). On the APPHOST deployment (a second copy of this app,
# EMBED_MODE=1) set EMBED_PARENT_ORIGIN to this app's public origin —
# apphost refuses every route except /embed, so no login surface, no
# /api/v1/*, and no session cookies exist on that origin. EMBED_TOKEN_SECRET
# is the HMAC key shared by both deployments for embed tokens and export
# nonces (falls back to SECRET_KEY — fine for local dev; use a dedicated
# value when the two deployments are separate services).
# EMBED_ORIGIN=https://campus-apphost-development.up.railway.app
# EMBED_MODE=1
# EMBED_PARENT_ORIGIN=https://<classroom-dev-domain>
# EMBED_TOKEN_SECRET=shared-hmac-key
